                  %a{:href => "#celestial_amplitudes_and_celestial_holography"} Celestial amplitudes and celestial holography
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em flat space holography
            is a – somewhat more hypothetical – generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            in the form of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotically
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulks"} bulks
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotically
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowskian
          %blockquote
            %p
              In order to still relate this to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
              notice that the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/far+horizon+geometry"} far horizon geometry
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS
              branes is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+orbifold"} flat orbifold
              spacetime (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "near-horizon+geometry#FarHorizonGeometry"} there
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck scale
              for single branes (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone+branes"}> cone branes
              ”), hence in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+1%2FN+limit"} large 1/N limit
              (opposite to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
              in which the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
              applies).
          %p
            In one more well-developed version of flat space holography,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotically
            flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            are related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theories"} conformal field theories
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/celestial+spheres"} celestial spheres
            in two dimensions lower – “celestial amplitudes”. This goes back to an observation in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#deBoerSolodukhin03"} de Boer &amp; Solodukhin 2003
